    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0282" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg270"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851D.001/22: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Cayenne</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">LaMont</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cayenne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-29T08:00:00-04:00">March 29, 1943—8
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 3—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–41. Reference my telegram No. 25 March 23, 7 p.m.<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d236-f1"/> and telegram No. 286 [<hi rendition="#italic">287?</hi>]
                    of March 26, 1943 from Singer of the Army, Paramaribo, to Singer, [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] Cayenne for Colonel Le Bel and the American
                    Consul, Cayenne, which was repeated to the Department and which quoted a message
                    from General de Gaulle to Sophie, Mayor of Cayenne.</p>
                <p>Yesterday Mr. Sophie showed me a copy of a telegram which he sent to General de
                    Gaulle in the name of the temporary committee, requesting him to withdraw the
                    nomination of Bertaud as Governor of French Guiana inasmuch as with the arrival
                    of Rapenne the colony now has a Governor.</p>
                <pb facs="0283" n="271" xml:id="pg271"/>
                <p>The temporary committee disbanded upon the arrival of Colonel Le Bel and only met
                    yesterday to agree upon the above mentioned telegram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">LaMont</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d236-f1" n="56" xml:id="d236-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 25 not in Department files. The Department transmitted it to the
                    Office of Strategic Services.</p>
            </note>
